# Subagent scratch. Agents doing the Þorláksbiblía ø retrofit write throwaway
# locating crops before the real windowed read, and several have dropped them
# into a `_work/` HERE rather than in the campaign's own `_work/`, which lives
# in the sibling C:\Projects\Hexapla-releases and is not a git repo at all.
# One such crop reached `git status` on 2026-09-06 and had to be caught by hand
# before the commit. Nothing in this repo's `_work/` is project content.
_work/

# Correspondence drafts — PERSONAL, never commit (owner instruction 2026-07-27).
# These are permission/enquiry emails to third parties and contain other
# people's names and contact addresses. 17 of them had been tracked and were
# PUBLIC on GitHub until they were purged from history on 2026-07-27; the
# purge is only durable if they stay ignored. Keep them on disk, out of git.
store-assets/*_draft.txt
store-assets/*_drafts.txt
store-assets/*draft*.txt
store-assets/*_reply*.txt

# /doctor settings backup — local artifact, not project content.
CLAUDE.md.doctor-backup

# Timestamped working backups (foo.py.bak-0823). Local scratch from long
# editing sessions; the history is in git, not in these.
*.bak-*

